        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.2.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.2.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " Almighty says, “I have heard the people of Moab and Ammon insulting and taunting my people, and boasting that they would seize their land. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.2.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.2.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ZEP 2:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "GEN.19.24"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Gen 19.24",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As surely as I am the living ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.2.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.2.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", the God of Israel, I swear that Moab and Ammon are going to be destroyed like Sodom and Gomorrah. They will become a place of salt pits and everlasting ruin, overgrown with weeds. Those of my people who survive will plunder them and take their land.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ZEP.2.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ZEP.2.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
